    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "## 3.4 Missing Value Handling Justification\n",
        "\n",
        "The `room_type` attribute contained 906 missing values. These values were handled according to the patient's admission status. When `admitted` was equal to 0, the missing room type was replaced with `Not Applicable` because a room is not required for a patient who was not admitted. When `admitted` was equal to 1 but the room type was missing, it was replaced with `Unknown` because the patient was admitted, but the specific room category was not recorded.\n",
        "\n",
        "This approach preserves all 1,000 records and distinguishes structurally unavailable values from genuinely unknown values. Deleting the `room_type` column or removing records with missing values would cause unnecessary information loss."
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "Og1zgQ-HDXx-"
      }
    },
