        "## 3.12 Outlier Handling Justification\n",
        "\n",
        "Potential outliers in the main clinical numerical attributes were identified using the Interquartile Range (IQR) method. The identified values were also compared against reasonable clinical ranges. No impossible clinical values were detected.\n",
        "\n",
        "The IQR-identified values were retained because extreme blood pressure, blood sugar, cholesterol, and BMI measurements may represent genuine high-risk patients. Removing or replacing these values could eliminate important information required for predicting `disease_risk_level`. Therefore, only clearly invalid values would be treated as data errors, while clinically possible extreme values were preserved."
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "yLeVglmFGJ7f"
      }
    },
