    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "## 3.15 Feature Engineering Justification\n",
        "\n",
        "The `appointment_date` attribute was transformed into `appointment_year`, `appointment_month`, and `appointment_day_of_week`. Machine-learning models cannot directly interpret a complete date value effectively, so extracting these components produces usable numerical features that may represent time-related patterns.\n",
        "\n",
        "`pulse_pressure` was calculated as the difference between systolic and diastolic blood pressure. `mean_arterial_pressure` was calculated using both blood-pressure measurements to represent the average pressure within the arteries. These derived measurements may provide additional information about cardiovascular health.\n",
        "\n",
        "The continuous `age` and `bmi` attributes were also grouped into meaningful categories. The new `age_group` and `bmi_category` features may help the model identify non-linear risk patterns among different age and body-mass-index groups. The original numerical attributes were retained to avoid losing detailed information."
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "5GMrHRCvG5CQ"
      }
    },
