      "source": [
        "## 3.17 Feature Selection Justification\n",
        "\n",
        "Thirteen demographic and clinical features were selected for predicting `disease_risk_level`. The selected attributes describe patient age, gender, diagnosis, previous admission history, blood pressure, blood sugar, cholesterol, BMI, and the newly engineered clinical features.\n",
        "\n",
        "Identifiers such as `record_id` and `patient_id` were excluded because their values do not describe patient health. The alternative targets `no_show` and `readmitted_30_days` were excluded to prevent target leakage. Appointment, room, payment, and billing attributes were not selected because they mainly describe hospital operations and financial activities rather than the patient's clinical disease risk. This domain-based selection reduces irrelevant information and keeps the model focused on meaningful health-related factors."
